{"timestamp": 1779396536.043766, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 17, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I reported Alice\u2019s body in medbay, right on/near the scan area. I did not see Diana\u2019s body myself.\n\nMy route was navigation -> storage -> medbay -> electrical -> back to medbay. I saw Charlie in storage around ticks 4-6; he came in from medbay and later left toward lower engine. I saw Eve enter medbay from electrical around tick 10, and Alice entered medbay from upper engine around tick 11. Alice was alive in medbay at tick 12 when I left. Then I went to electrical, saw Frank come into electrical from medbay at tick 15, and he left toward cafeteria at tick 16. When I returned to medbay, Alice was dead.\n\nSo the people I\u2019d want to hear from are Eve and Frank especially, since they were around medbay close to when Alice died."}}
{"timestamp": 1779396561.53911, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 17, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "My route was weapons -> security -> electrical -> medbay -> storage. I saw Diana enter weapons from security around tick 4, she was alive then, and I didn\u2019t see her again after that.\n\nI got to medbay around tick 10/11. I saw Bob there, and Alice entered medbay from upper engine at tick 11. So I can confirm Alice was alive then, and Bob\u2019s part about me being in medbay is true. I didn\u2019t stay long \u2014 I left toward storage and was there when the meeting got called.\n\nI did not see Frank at all this round, so if Bob saw Frank come from medbay into electrical around tick 15, that\u2019s definitely important. I\u2019d like to hear Frank explain that. Charlie also matters for Diana maybe, since Diana was last alive near weapons/security early and Charlie was apparently around storage/engine side."}}
{"timestamp": 1779396648.6408, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 17, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I can confirm Bob's timeline for my movement. I came through medbay into electrical around tick 14/15. When I ran through medbay, Alice was very much alive. I didn't stop, just passed through to electrical, saw Bob, and then headed up to cafeteria. \n\nIf Alice died right after I left, the killer must have slipped in from upper engine or storage right behind me... or honestly Bob, you going back to medbay right after I left and \"finding\" her dead is a little convenient. \n\nAs for Diana, I was top side doing tasks in upper engine and oxygen early on, so I didn't see her or whoever got her around security/weapons. I want to hear what Charlie was doing, since he might have been near the right side of the map."}}
{"timestamp": 1779396675.2035542, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 17, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "My route was electrical -> medbay -> storage -> lower engine -> upper engine. I only really saw Bob this round: he came into storage from navigation around tick 4 and we were both in storage for a few ticks. I did come into storage from medbay like Bob said, then I left down toward lower engine. I never saw Alice or Diana alive, and I didn\u2019t see any bodies.\n\nFor Alice: based on everyone\u2019s stories, Eve and Bob both have Alice alive around 11/12, and Frank is the last person claiming he saw Alice alive while coming out of medbay around 14/15. Then Bob finds her dead right after. That puts the strongest suspicion on Frank or possibly Bob self-reporting, but Frank\u2019s timing is the tightest if Bob really saw him coming from medbay.\n\nFor Diana: Eve last saw Diana alive near weapons/security early. I was on left/lower side after storage, so I don\u2019t think I\u2019m useful there. Frank saying he was top side oxygen/upper engine early could also put him somewhat near that side, depending on exact timing, but not enough by itself.\n\nI think Frank is the most suspicious from the Alice kill timing, with Bob as the only other real possibility if it\u2019s a self-report."}}
{"timestamp": 1779396698.141536, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 17, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I\u2019ll restate the key point: Frank confirms he came from medbay into electrical at tick 15, and he confirms he saw me in electrical. That means I wasn\u2019t in medbay at that moment.\n\nAlice was alive when I left medbay around tick 12. Eve saw that too. Then Frank is the next person we know came directly out of medbay, and immediately after that I go back and find Alice dead. Frank saying \u201cshe was alive when I passed\u201d is only his word, and nobody else can confirm that.\n\nSo from my perspective, it\u2019s very hard for this to be me unless you think I somehow killed Alice, left, got seen in electrical by Frank, and then came back to report. Frank had the cleanest opportunity on Alice. I think Frank is the vote here."}}
{"timestamp": 1779396725.686849, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 17, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I don\u2019t have anything new beyond my route, but putting it together: I saw Alice alive in medbay with Bob around tick 11, then I left to storage and stayed there until the meeting. I never saw Frank.\n\nFrank confirming he came from medbay into electrical right before Bob found Alice is the biggest thing. Since Frank also says he saw Bob in electrical, that makes Bob being in medbay at the kill moment less likely unless it was a very weird self-report timing. Frank\u2019s \u201cAlice was alive when I passed\u201d is only his word.\n\nFor Diana, I only saw her enter weapons from security at tick 4, alive. I don\u2019t know who killed her, but Frank\u2019s claimed top-side route doesn\u2019t really clear him there either.\n\nI\u2019m leaning Frank. If we vote wrong here it\u2019s dangerous, but based on Alice\u2019s timing, Frank has the clearest opportunity."}}
{"timestamp": 1779396748.665817, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 17, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "Listen to me carefully, Charlie and Eve. Bob is playing a very obvious framing game here. \n\nThink about the logic: I walked through Medbay at tick 14 and Alice was alive. I go straight into Electrical at tick 15/16 and run right into Bob. If I had just killed Alice, why on earth would I stroll directly into the adjacent room and show my face to Bob? I would have gone up to Cafeteria or back around to avoid being seen near the crime scene. \n\nInstead, look at what Bob did. He sees me leave Medbay. He knows I'm the perfect scapegoat. So he immediately walks back into Medbay, kills Alice himself, and instantly self-reports to lock in the frame job. He\u2019s pushing so hard for my elimination because he needs this setup to work. \n\nAlso, regarding Diana: I was top side (Upper Engine/Oxygen/Cafeteria) the whole early game. I was nowhere near Weapons/Security where Eve last saw Diana. \n\nBob is the killer, and he's using my confirmed route to hand-deliver a frame job. I am voting Bob. If you vote me, the Duck wins. If you aren't 100% sure, skip, but Bob's instant return to Medbay is a blatant self-report."}}
{"timestamp": 1779396770.745902, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 17, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "My info hasn\u2019t changed: I only saw Bob in storage early, and that lines up with what Bob said about me. I have no direct body info.\n\nBut on the Alice kill, the timeline still points more to Frank than Bob to me. Eve confirms Alice was alive in medbay with Bob around 11. Bob leaves, Frank then admits he comes from medbay into electrical right before the report. The only proof Alice was alive when Frank passed is Frank\u2019s own word.\n\nFrank\u2019s self-report theory is possible, but it requires Bob to see Frank leave medbay, go back in immediately, kill Alice, and report perfectly to frame him. Meanwhile Frank was the confirmed last person coming out of the room where Alice died.\n\nAlso Frank\u2019s \u201cwhy would I show my face\u201d argument doesn\u2019t clear him \u2014 if he killed in medbay, leaving into electrical and claiming she was alive is exactly the kind of defense he\u2019d have to make.\n\nI\u2019m still leaning Frank as the best vote."}}
